// Pianoteq 9 piano adapter for the shared plugin pack, a thin layer over the
// builtin `piano("default", {...})` convention. This module owns the alias the
// builtin resolves and the alias-backed settings record. The instrument, its
// license and the `.state` dump belong to the composer; this library ships
// neither plugin binaries nor preset state.
//
// Alias: `default` -> the installed Pianoteq VST3 in plugins.json; `piano()`
// uses it unless the source names another plugin. Upstream: Pianoteq 9,
// proprietary (Modartt), sold per edition and instrument pack.
//
// A device's `state:` path resolves against the .muz file that declares it, and a
// function body evaluates in its defining module, so keep the piano() call and
// the path in your own module:
//
//     piano("default", pianoteq.settings("assets/piano/bechstein-warm.state"))
let alias = "default";

fn settings(state, overrides = {}) = merge({state: state}, overrides);
